"""Copy this file to app/ical_feeds_data.py (gitignored — it'll hold real,
somewhat-sensitive calendar URLs) and fill in FEEDS with your real listings,
then run:

    python -m app.add_ical_feed

Each entry:
  cluster           - exact cluster name as it appears in the app (case-sensitive)
  category          - "ac" or "nonac"
  source            - "airbnb", "booking_com", "oyo", or "makemytrip"
  url               - the calendar export (.ics) URL from that platform
  label             - optional, but recommended once you have more than one
                       feed per cluster+category (e.g. multiple Airbnb
                       accounts) so you can tell them apart in Admin -> Automation
  managed_by_email  - optional; email of an EXISTING team member this account
                       belongs to. Create the user first (Admin -> Users or
                       `python -m app.create_user`) — a feed can't be mapped
                       to a user that doesn't exist yet. Run
                       `python -m app.add_ical_feed --list-users` to see who's
                       already in the system.
"""

